  "power": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "datasheet-table - JNP10K-PWR-AC2 5.5 kW each as the family guides; the AC/AC3/DC variants are gaps. The MX10008/MX10016 datasheet states typical power consumption 23 kW, fully loaded, naming no ambient or side - carried as power-typical-w. The guide works an example of 28,000 W for sixteen MX10K-LC2101 in a redundant configuration (5200 W + 22,800 W) - a sample, not carried"
  },
  "rear": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - g050702 (isometric, fractions only): one full-height column of ten JNP10K-PWR supplies at the left, two full-height fan trays right. Base configuration ships five supplies; all ten bays are drawn. Each supply bay is 91.4 x 88.9 mm, the JNP10K-PWR-AC2 as the guide's Table 39 gives it (3.6 in. wide, 3.5 in. high; guide page 107), and the ten stand one above the next with no gap, as Figure 2 draws them, the earthing terminal's strip below PSU 9. The bays were 84.0 x 91.0 mm, spread over the fan trays' height. The guide's Table 7 gives the fan trays 6.6 in. (16.8 cm, about 167.6 mm) wide and 36.6 in. (92.97 cm) high (guide pages 32 to 33), and juniper/jnp10016-fan@2 and juniper/jnp10016-fan2@2 are drawn at that size; juniper/jnp10016-fan@1 and juniper/jnp10016-fan2@1, 176 x 924 mm from the drawing, are kept for a saved rack that names them. The two fan bays are 167.6 x 929.6 mm and stand against the supply column and against each other, centred in the 930 mm height (y 0.2). 91.4 + 2 x 167.6 mm is 426.6 mm of the 442 mm body, and no figure shows the other 15.4 mm, so it is left empty at the right edge, an estimate"
  },
